NOTICE
======

mymc-py is a Python 3 port of, and is substantially derived from, the
following public-domain work:

    "mymc" / "ps2mc" - PlayStation 2 memory card image utilities
    By Ross Ridge
    Public Domain
    Original (Python 2) source: https://sourceforge.net/p/mymc-opl/code/

Ross Ridge also authored the "PlayStation 2 Memory Card File System"
specification document (public domain) that this implementation follows:
https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2/blob/master/pcsx2/Reference/PS2-MemoryCardFileSystem.htm

The ECC routines were also ported (as "CalculateECC") into PCSX2 and its
derivatives (including AetherSX2), which is why .ps2 images produced by this
project are directly compatible with those emulators.

The Python 3 port, the command-line interface, the folder-save "build-card"
tool, the validation tool and the tests are additional work licensed under
the MIT License (see LICENSE).

This product includes software developed by Ross Ridge
(http://mymc.berlios.de, public domain).